# CODEOWNERS: who GitHub asks to review which files.
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-security-and-analysis/about-code-owners
#
# A pull request that touches a path below automatically requests a review from
# that path's owner. This only *blocks* merging when branch protection turns on
# "Require review from Code Owners". Without that rule it routes reviews; it
# does not gate them.
#
# Two things silently break a CODEOWNERS file, so check both:
#   - An owner without write access to the repository is ignored.
#   - Later rules win. The last matching line decides, not the most specific
#     one (the opposite of .gitignore).
#
# On clone: replace @Joehmyers throughout with your own handles or @org/team
# names. A file full of someone else's username is worse than no file.

# Default owner for anything not matched below.
*                   @Joehmyers

# Agent configuration. Permissions, hooks, skills, and subagent definitions
# decide what an agent may do without asking a human first. Review changes here
# with the same care as any other security configuration.
/.claude/           @Joehmyers
/AGENTS.md          @Joehmyers
/CLAUDE.md          @Joehmyers

# Verification and CI. Everything else trusts these scripts when they say the
# repo is green, so a weakened check is a silent loss of coverage.
/ops/               @Joehmyers
/.github/           @Joehmyers

# Decisions. Accepted records are immutable: a change here is either a new
# record or a mistake.
/docs/decisions/    @Joehmyers
